defmodule PlaywrightEx.BrowserContext do
  @moduledoc ~S"""
  BrowserContexts provide a way to operate multiple independent browser sessions.

  If a page opens another page, e.g. with a `window.open` call, the popup will belong to the parent page's browser
  context.

  Playwright allows creating isolated non-persistent browser contexts with `PlaywrightEx.Browser.new_context/2` method. Non-persistent browser
  contexts don't write any browsing data to disk.

  ```elixir
  # Create a new incognito browser context
  context = Browser.new_context!(browser)
  # Create a new page inside context.
  page = BrowserContext.new_page!(context)
  Page.goto!(page, "https://example.com")
  # Dispose context once it's no longer needed.
  BrowserContext.close!(context)
  ```

  *Since Playwright 1.8.*

  ## Events

  ### `:background_page`

  *Since Playwright 1.11.* This event is not emitted.

  ### `:close`

  Emitted when Browser context gets closed. This might happen because of one of the following:

  * Browser context is closed.
  * Browser application is closed or crashed.
  * The `PlaywrightEx.Browser.close/2` method was called.

  ### `:console`

  *Since Playwright 1.34.* Emitted when JavaScript within the page calls one of console API methods, e.g. `console.log` or `console.dir`.

  The arguments passed into `console.log` and the page are available on the [`ConsoleMessage`](`PlaywrightEx.ConsoleMessage`) event handler argument.

  **Usage**

  ```elixir
  BrowserContext.on(context, :console, fn msg ->
    values = for arg <- ConsoleMessage.args(msg), do: JSHandle.json_value!(arg)
    IO.puts(inspect(values))
  end)

  Page.evaluate!(page, "() => console.log('hello', 5, { foo: 'bar' })")
  ```

  ### `:dialog`

  *Since Playwright 1.34.* Emitted when a JavaScript dialog appears, such as `alert`, `prompt`, `confirm` or `beforeunload`. Listener **must** either `PlaywrightEx.Dialog.accept/2` or `PlaywrightEx.Dialog.dismiss/1` the dialog - otherwise the page will [freeze](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/EventLoop#never_blocking) waiting for the dialog, and actions like click will never finish.

  **Usage**

  ```elixir
  BrowserContext.on(context, :dialog, fn dialog ->
    Dialog.accept(dialog)
  end)
  ```

  > #### Note {: .info}
  >
  > When no [`Page.on(:dialog)`](PlaywrightEx.Page.html#module-dialog) or [`BrowserContext.on(:dialog)`](PlaywrightEx.BrowserContext.html#module-dialog) listeners are present, all dialogs are automatically dismissed.

  ### `:dialog_closed`

  *Since Playwright 1.63.* Emitted when a JavaScript dialog in any page belonging to this context has been closed, either by `PlaywrightEx.Dialog.accept/2`, by `PlaywrightEx.Dialog.dismiss/1`, or manually by the user in the headed browser.

  ### `:download`

  *Since Playwright 1.60.* Emitted when attachment download started in any page belonging to this context. User can access basic file operations on downloaded content via the passed [`Download`](`PlaywrightEx.Download`) instance. See also [`Page.on(:download)`](PlaywrightEx.Page.html#module-download) to receive events about a specific page.

  ### `:frame_attached`

  *Since Playwright 1.60.* Emitted when a frame is attached in any page belonging to this context. See also [`Page.on(:frame_attached)`](PlaywrightEx.Page.html#module-frame_attached) to receive events about a specific page.

  ### `:frame_detached`

  *Since Playwright 1.60.* Emitted when a frame is detached in any page belonging to this context. See also [`Page.on(:frame_detached)`](PlaywrightEx.Page.html#module-frame_detached) to receive events about a specific page.

  ### `:frame_navigated`

  *Since Playwright 1.60.* Emitted when a frame is navigated to a new url in any page belonging to this context. See also [`Page.on(:frame_navigated)`](PlaywrightEx.Page.html#module-frame_navigated) to receive events about navigations in a specific page.

  ### `:page`

  The event is emitted when a new Page is created in the BrowserContext. The page may still be loading. The event will
  also fire for popup pages. See also [`Page.on(:popup)`](PlaywrightEx.Page.html#module-popup) to receive events about popups relevant to a specific page.

  The earliest moment that page is available is when it has navigated to the initial url. For example, when opening a
  popup with `window.open('http://example.com')`, this event will fire when the network request to "http://example.com" is
  done and its response has started loading in the popup. If you would like to route/listen to this network request, use `PlaywrightEx.BrowserContext.route/4` and [`BrowserContext.on(:request)`](PlaywrightEx.BrowserContext.html#module-request) respectively instead of similar methods on the [`Page`](`PlaywrightEx.Page`).

  ```elixir
